fix(scripts): make the specs gate POSIX, because it broke signing

The gate shipped as `#!/usr/bin/env bash`. This repository sets core.hooksPath,
so the pre-commit hook that calls it runs WHEREVER git runs in this repository —
including inside the MCP's container, which is Alpine and has no bash.

Every signed commit on this machine began failing:

    INVARIANT_VIOLATION: signing: gitsign refused to sign: exit status 1
    env: can't execute 'bash': No such file or directory

A gate that breaks signing is worse than the hole it closes. It was found by the
next commit after the gate merged — which is lucky rather than by design: the
gate's own self-test runs on a machine that has bash, so nothing about it was
going to catch this.

`#!/bin/sh` and `set -u` without `pipefail`, which is not POSIX. The pipelines
are greps whose failure is a normal "found nothing". Verified by running it
under Alpine's sh with no bash present, and by signing this commit.

The other gates are bash too and are untouched: none of them is wired into a git
hook, so none has ever run anywhere but a developer machine or CI. The moment
one is, it needs this same treatment.

